      "title": "The other side of it",
      "body": "I went around the branch to see what he was looking at. He went around to see what I was looking at. We met where I had started. Neither of us wanted to be the first to ask.",
      "decision": "hold",
      "reason": "Concrete fictional timing is permissible, but the image has only one seahorse and supplies no particular clue to this encounter. The mutual movement also approaches existing tail-space courtship and branch insecurity material. A real pair composition could strengthen it; do not replace held earlier pair text.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Second seahorse, mutual circling and conversation invented; photograph supplies only narrator and branch."
    },
    {
      "characterId": "rue-ribbon",
      "sourceIndices": [
        5,
        6
      ],
      "title": "Before I knew what it meant",
      "body": "When I was small, a fish stopped in front of my mouth. I waited for it to say something. It waited for me to stop looking hungry. We both grew uncomfortable without either of us having made a decision.",
      "decision": "hold",
      "reason": "Actual black juvenile supports childhood, but this repeats admitted My mouth was already open and Before the blue. The unseen visitor does not add a distinct enough consequence.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Visitor and waiting sequence fictional, black juvenile appearance visible. No claim of rapid color or sex change."
    }
  ],
